From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:49:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: refuse an output configured with no size

An output the device's configuration enables, output 0 through xres and
yres and any output through outputs[n].xres and outputs[n].yres, takes
its size from there, and nothing checks that the size is not zero. The
guest is then told of an enabled output with a zero width or height, a
size no monitor has, while the EDID made for it falls back to QEMU's
default of 1280x800 there.

Refuse such an output at realize, as an output with an xres but no yres
already is.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
index 270fbaae10..23dfe7e51e 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
@@ -225,6 +225,14 @@ virtio_gpu_base_device_realize(DeviceState *qdev,
         }
     }
 
+    for (i = 0; i < g->conf.max_outputs; i++) {
+        if ((g->enabled_output_bitmask & (1 << i)) &&
+            (!g->req_state[i].width || !g->req_state[i].height)) {
+            error_setg(errp, "output %d has a zero xres or yres", i);
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
     if (virtio_gpu_virgl_enabled(g->conf)) {
         error_setg(&g->migration_blocker, "virgl is not yet migratable");
         if (migrate_add_blocker(&g->migration_blocker, errp) < 0) {
